{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["And he fashioned it with a graving tool — he took the gold from each one's hand and gathered it and tied it all in a garment until they made a mold of clay and of wax in the manner of metal casters, and made in it the shape of a calf, and cast the gold into it, and it became a calf, as written: ואשליכהו באש ויצא העגל הזה. And it is written: ויצר ככרים כסף בשני חריטים." "These are your gods, O Israel, who brought you up — were they such fools that they did not know that this calf, born today, did not bring them up from Egypt? All idol worshippers know that our Elohim in heaven created the world; but in this they erred — that the terafim have in them an unclean spirit, just as prophets have in them a holy spirit, and they supposed that the calf, which was speaking through an unclean spirit, was as though speaking through a holy spirit from above. Therefore they say: אלה אלהיך ישראל אשר העלוך — that is, it has in it a holy spirit, and it is as though a holy spirit goes before us. So too Laban said of the terafim: למה גנבת את אלהי. And to test Israel through it, He put in it an unclean spirit, so that all kinds of sorcery and ov and yidoni had power through it to oppose the heavenly entourage and to tell things before they come to be — to know whether they would be wholehearted toward YHWH their Elohim and there would not be in them a soothsayer or diviner or sorcerer, and none who believes in a sign or portent of an unclean spirit, as written: כי מנסה ה׳ אלהיכם אתכם לדעת הישכם אוהבים את ה׳ אלהיכם וגו׳."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:46.431486566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}